do one Lethal damage. Lethal is a 4 dot spell, I have 4 dots in Mind, so I have 1 free Reach. They aren't going to stand there for 3 hours to let me gather my spell, so I use my one Reach for that. I'm pretty quick, so I'll have it still based on Touch (Dexterity + Brawl - Defense). Damage is 'lasting' so I don't need to use Duration. Scale is still one Subject, Size 5. The big thing is Potency. With Gnosis 2, Mind 4, my dicepool is going to be 6, to do 1 damage (as I have 1 Potency, default). For every point of Potency I add, my dicepool gets -2. I can use a Yantra to up my dicepool, but a yantra must be semiotically linked to the spell. Some Storytellers go easy on this but Charlaquin made a good list of what yantras can be. Your Gnosis determines the maximum amount of Yantras you can use, but you only get one for 'free' and the others take an extra turn of spellcasting, which is pretty prohibitive for fighting (though note you can cast a quick spell to keep an opponent away, then use that time to prepare a more powerful one). For this example, the spell is Mind Flay, and my character has a bone skinning knife, because I don't know why, that counts as their Path tool. This gives them a +1. With a dicepool of seven I can guarantee that 1 Lethal damage, but I could conceivably up my Potency by 3, giving me -6, and a Dicepool of 1, then cast with Willpower, for a 'good chance' with 4 dice. Now that penalties have been figured out, my wife reminds me that the spell's Primary Factor is Potency, so I get a +3 to the Potency (your Arcana -1), making the total Potency 7. Then I roll to touch, and potentially Mind Flay them. I could have risked Paradox to make the spell cast Sensory, and I wouldn't require a touch roll and could just zap them.<br /> <br /> If I succeed in this spell, I do 7 Lethal Damage. The Potency is set for damage. I don't get any extras based on how many Successes I roll (there is a potential exception in this with Exceptional Successes).<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7079_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7079\" data-vbnamecard=\"7079\">Marcus</a> I think that's a neat idea, but considering the variation you find among vampires and mages, just one match might not cover it.<br /> <br /> I think I got this right, I know there's a lot of potential exceptions, like praxes and rotes but this seems correct for the basic spellcasting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really, Thank you for your explanation. Probably I'm not inside this mechanics but still it doesn't seems to me a great deal for a combat vampire (I'm talking about combat vampire since we are consodering damage spell). I mean, with resilence I could avoid the great part of the damage refkexively and deal my blow or kiss. What am I missing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-02T05:21:47-07:00","id":1136559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1136212-vampire-vs-mages?p=1136325#post1136325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We could do an experiment:<br /> <br /> - One give a setting (environment(Alley, Trafficated road, forest...), situation (combat, social... ) XP cap)<br /> <br /> - one create and play a Mage<br /> <br /> - one create and play a Vampire<br /> <br /> And play: scenario per scenario. Could be fun?<br /> <br /> Edit: Master would be anyone well aware of the rules for both the setting but nor Mage player neither Vampire.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This, but for a good study, there should be several attempts. Let's say a given number of players. Half create a vampire each with those conditions, the other half create a mage each, then pair them off in a 1v1 rpg battlle to the death (or, other ways of ending the conflict in one's favour). Observe the matchups, create a tier list and a strategy guide for the scenario no one will ever play again.<br /> <br /> I'd read the fuck out of that thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7104-s-brechen","name":"S. Brechen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-02T05:31:53-07:00","id":1136561,"title":"","content":"Space magic is probably the most annoying one. 3 dots of that and you can swing at them only for it to turn out, whoops, they're <i>not actually there</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-02T11:06:35-07:00","id":1136641,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1136212-vampire-vs-mages?p=1136527#post1136527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really, Thank you for your explanation. Probably I'm not inside this mechanics but still it doesn't seems to me a great deal for a combat vampire (I'm talking about combat vampire since we are consodering damage spell). I mean, with resilence I could avoid the great part of the damage refkexively and deal my blow or kiss. What am I missing?</div> </div> </div> </div>Mages can also take advantage of the usual banes for vampires, and probably at a lesser arcana. You wouldn't need to 'fireball' a vampire, when you can just set the entire room aflame, for instance.<br /> <br /> Elfive has it right, too, Space magic allows you to cast spells beyond sensory range, at sympathetic range, through connections they have with others. Time magic can also let you rewind things, so if a fight has gone bad, they can back up and try again. Providing they get the spell off.<br /> <br /> Space is the big thing, because you can do it in the comfort of your own home, getting all the yantra bonuses you want, taking extra time to make it a ritual spell.. A lot of people underestimate the importance of the sympathetic yantras, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-02T13:19:17-07:00","id":1136700,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1136212-vampire-vs-mages?p=1136641#post1136641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mages can also take advantage of the usual banes for vampires, and probably at a lesser arcana. You wouldn't need to 'fireball' a vampire, when you can just set the entire room aflame, for instance.<br /> <br /> Elfive has it right, too, Space magic allows you to cast spells beyond sensory range, at sympathetic range, through connections they have with others. Time magic can also let you rewind things, so if a fight has gone bad, they can back up and try again. Providing they get the spell off.<br /> <br /> Space is the big thing, because you can do it in the comfort of your own home, getting all the yantra bonuses you want, taking extra time to make it a ritual spell.. A lot of people underestimate the importance of the sympathetic yantras, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, once a Mage gets a decent Sympathetic Yantra (and has Space 2, obviously), Scry-and-Die becomes the major danger. Time 2 can do similarly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-02T15:40:44-07:00","id":1136739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1136212-vampire-vs-mages?p=1136561#post1136561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Space magic is probably the most annoying one. 3 dots of that and you can swing at them only for it to turn out, whoops, they're <i>not actually there</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Don\u00b4t forget Fate aka &quot;I see a stake in your future&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-02T15:44:30-07:00","id":1136740,"title":"","content":"&quot;Here's a souvenir I brought back from a trip to china. Where it's currently noon.&quot;<br /> *teleport'd*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-02T15:57:26-07:00","id":1136742,"title":"","content":"Lets please not make out that it's that easy or that everyone can do it, or we're back on the train with vampires with every discipline at their disposal and armies of silver-armored police. Space and Time are very useful against vampires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-02-2017, 07:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-02T16:16:18-07:00","id":1136743,"title":"","content":"Actually thinking about it you might just be able to shoot sunlight from a scrying window...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-02T21:05:40-07:00","id":1136816,"title":"","content":"Usually the power gap between single powers is so huge it's not even worth comparing them. 3dots in an arcana are usually as strong or stronger than 4 or 5 dots in a discipline or devotion. <br /> <br /> However setting and contest of the battle change things a little, I link to u an interesting discussion where I explained my points... <br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1135965-do-mages-need-a-bit-of-a-nerf-to-bring-them-in-line/page6\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...-in-line/page6</a><br /> <br /> Consider this_<br /> If vampires have the surprise advantage, time for prep and the situation allows for ambush, obfuscate and surprise attack, they can win and probably will. Mages without armor and magical shielding are very, very weak. <br /> <br /> If mages know what's coming for them, have time to get ready or the situation allows them to be the ones ahead of the race, they will probably level and annihilate every supernatural of any other splat. Unless said supernaturals have really really powerful Allies (ancient ghosts or powerful spirits, other mages...) or are Really REALLY fucking strong (in the case of vampires, metuselah level). <br /> <br /> @Marcus<br /> <br /> Thing is, if u are thinking about straight fighting like gangrel or daeva do, mage don't even need to get close to u or draw a gun to fuck you up. Space time and fate, heck even matter or forces means the mage won't even be a target for vampires...<br /> <br /> <br /> If anyones interested, I can also link an old discussion where my cabal of players had to face a coterie and their ghouls to free a mage hostage. That might show a little of what I mean.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4247,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4247-lasombra","user":"Lasombra","date":". 09-03-2017, 12:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4247-lasombra","name":"Lasombra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-03T04:06:55-07:00","id":1136879,"title":"","content":"A *highly specialized* Vampire can wreck havok on a Mage. It involved Resolve 5, Sorcerous Eunich, Coda Against Sorcery 5, Lance's Special FS, and Obfuscate 3+ (all doable at creation). It involves the Kindred having initiative and not losing like a chump on the Clash of Wills, even then. Coda and Sorcerous Eunich *might* apply to Clash of Wills?<br /> <br /> You still need to worry about spells that have no Withstand and do not target you, for instance Ban. Obfiscate comes into play there, where the idea is they never see you coming. This doesn't help against Magey McBuffaton, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-03T06:28:56-07:00","id":1136916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1136212-vampire-vs-mages?p=1136879#post1136879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A *highly specialized* Vampire can wreck havok on a Mage. It involved Resolve 5, Sorcerous Eunich, Coda Against Sorcery 5, Lance's Special FS, and Obfuscate 3+ (all doable at creation). It involves the Kindred having initiative and not losing like a chump on the Clash of Wills, even then. Coda and Sorcerous Eunich *might* apply to Clash of Wills?<br /> <br /> You still need to worry about spells that have no Withstand and do not target you, for instance Ban. Obfiscate comes into play there, where the idea is they never see you coming. This doesn't help against Magey McBuffaton, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mages has many more means of going about un noticed than obfuscate. What makes you so sure you will be able to surprise/spot one who doesnt want to be found?<br /> <br /> Forces Invis, Mind Incognito, Death veiling vs vampires, Prime veiling vs everything, Spirit mages probably in twilight. Nearly every path has some means of going about undetected if needs be except maybe an Acanthus but with them having Time and all, good luck surprising them.<br /> <br /> I mean sure, i bet anybody can make a splat that is solely built to fight a mage and it might win but the point is mages DONT need to be built soley to fight any other splat, they are versatile enough that if smart have many ways to defeat or escape any threat, before during or even after its happened.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-03T08:22:42-07:00","id":1136939,"title":"","content":"Why is this even under debate? I don't get it. Mages are openly acknoweldged to have more advantages than pretty much any other splat out there. Even if it wasn't for the power of their Arcana at high levels, they specialize in information gathering and shielding. While I'm all for claiming we shouldn't ignore vampire mystics who can predict the future or a vampire's ability to call upon a covenant, mages get the exact same considerations PLUS the ablity obscure what they're doing so the vampires don't know. <br /> <br /> Most of the time, a vamp and mage will come into conflict is if the vampire accidentily infringes on the mage's territory and the mage senses it and does something about it. The vampire, likely trying to feed on a sleepwalker, is probably going to be caught off guard because they can't sense the mage back by default, whereas any of the vamp's hunting tools are easily pinged by Passive Mage Sight at minimum. The scenario will flop around a lot, but the mage is almost always going to be the one who wins simply because they'll be quicker to figure out a vamp is around than the vamp realizing the mage is.<br /> <br /> <br /> In any wartime / battle scenario, information is king. Mages specialize in information. That means the Awakened will usually win. The only situation that vampries come out ahead is in the field of long term mind control, and even then its a shaky lead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-03T12:58:12-07:00","id":1137001,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I don't see this disparity that is getting so much attention. Yes, if the mage has plenty of time to prepare and everything goes his way and all the arcana fall into place etc; sure. Odd game you are playing, though, where the mage gets to plan a slow hit on the vamp without any plot complications.<br /> <br /> Much is made of the unmaking spells, for instance. Instakill buttons are scary. But to get there, a mage needs a) 5 dots in an arcanum and b) 5 dots in gnosis. A comparable leech is scary as hell. Even before any disciplines are added, a vampire with 5 BP in frenzy can add 15 to any physical dicepool. One sniper bullet out of the mage's sensory range/thrown barstool in range and he is likely toast - even for a vampire with no dots in the relevant abilities. Or 15 dots to sneak up (or merely 10 if you rule the current frenzy supercedes the ability to be a stealthy predator) before adding any natural skills. If you get close enough for the grapple, that +15 dice is v. likely to give you an exceptional success - which means an additional +5 damage due to blood loss if you apply the feed move. Depending on how you take the wording, a 5BP vampire should get an additional +5 to either stamina or all withstand ratings in frenzy. Even an unprepared vampire in a physical confrontation is terrifying, and almost certainly lethal, to most mages if they get within grabbing distance. And this is all before you apply disciplines, ghoul hordes etc.<br /> <br /> Of course, if the mage is sniping from safety, the vampire might die. Vice versa, too, though. If the sniper rifle from a helicopter doesn't take your fancy, how about the level 2 cruac ritual that kills any mortal at any distance by exploding their bowels (Shed the Virulent Bowels, I believe). Or some of the resist magic merits from the same.<br /> <br /> In my mage game? We had one obfuscate 3 vampire tear up two different mages - one with matter 4, one with death 4. We even had the death specialist immune to obfuscate with an improvised spell (the mage won the clash), but stellar stealth rolls meant the vampire got in there and stomped the mage in a grapple. Both mages ended up bloodbound in a cellar - for more drama ensuing. There is a chance in the next game that our acanthus is going to have a battle with some vamp heavy in fortitude, and I think trickiness is going to be more useful than any agg damage.<br /> <br /> Theoretically, sitting in my armchair, I know how to prevent a mugging. When it happens, I hope the muggers work out what I have planned for them, and are glad to go along with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":668,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/668-hoodedclaw","user":"hoodedclaw","date":". 09-03-2017, 04:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/668-hoodedclaw","name":"hoodedclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-03T13:42:08-07:00","id":1137013,"title":"","content":"This entire thread is pointless.<br /> <br /> vampire if you want to play politics, backstabbing, personal horror and favor exchange<br /> <br /> Mage if you want to play magical exploration and uncover secrets, encounter monsters and wtfs<br /> <br /> Versus wise depends on the scenario, a mage could engulf a vampire with fire using the Forces Arcana and call it a day, a vampire could seduce an unwary mage, drag him back to her haven and get that sweet, sweet awakened Vitae when he is most vulnerable","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","name":"Shawarbaaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-03T13:43:23-07:00","id":1137014,"title":"","content":"Edit: doubled post sorry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 09-03-2017, 04:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-03T13:44:37-07:00","id":1137016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hoodedclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1136212-vampire-vs-mages?p=1137001#post1137001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, I don't see this disparity that is getting so much attention. Yes, if the mage has plenty of time to prepare and everything goes his way and all the arcana fall into place etc; sure. Odd game you are playing, though, where the mage gets to plan a slow hit on the vamp without any plot complications.<br /> <br /> Much is made of the unmaking spells, for instance. Instakill buttons are scary. But to get there, a mage needs a) 5 dots in an arcanum and b) 5 dots in gnosis. A comparable leech is scary as hell. Even before any disciplines are added, a vampire with 5 BP in frenzy can add 15 to any physical dicepool. One sniper bullet out of the mage's sensory range/thrown barstool in range and he is likely toast - even for a vampire with no dots in the relevant abilities. Or 15 dots to sneak up (or merely 10 if you rule the current frenzy supercedes the ability to be a stealthy predator) before adding any natural skills. If you get close enough for the grapple, that +15 dice is v. likely to give you an exceptional success - which means an additional +5 damage due to blood loss if you apply the feed move. Depending on how you take the wording, a 5BP vampire should get an additional +5 to either stamina or all withstand ratings in frenzy. Even an unprepared vampire in a physical confrontation is terrifying, and almost certainly lethal, to most mages if they get within grabbing distance. And this is all before you apply disciplines, ghoul hordes etc.<br /> <br /> Of course, if the mage is sniping from safety, the vampire might die. Vice versa, too, though. If the sniper rifle from a helicopter doesn't take your fancy, how about the level 2 cruac ritual that kills any mortal at any distance by exploding their bowels (Shed the Virulent Bowels, I believe). Or some of the resist magic merits from the same.<br /> <br /> In my mage game? We had one obfuscate 3 vampire tear up two different mages - one with matter 4, one with death 4. We even had the death specialist immune to obfuscate with an improvised spell (the mage won the clash), but stellar stealth rolls meant the vampire got in there and stomped the mage in a grapple. Both mages ended up bloodbound in a cellar - for more drama ensuing. There is a chance in the next game that our acanthus is going to have a battle with some vamp heavy in fortitude, and I think trickiness is going to be more useful than any agg damage.<br /> <br /> Theoretically, sitting in my armchair, I know how to prevent a mugging. When it happens, I hope the muggers work out what I have planned for them, and are glad to go along with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's is exactly what I meant and why I proposed example scenarios to let the dice speaks. I mean, with celerity for the interrupt (that could calls for a clash of wills so that it is at least a play at par) a frenzy vampire with a little of vigor could annihilate a mage: damage for the bite plus vigor plus vitae loss.<br /> <br /> With resilence is possible to reflexively avoid res+1 lethal damages or res agg. Damages for those devastating spells. Even fireball or sunlight created by the mage. Without considering Juggernaut Gait.<br /> <br /> With interrupt and dominate/Majesty you can take control of the mage. Yes, it's true also the opposite but, as I said, is play at par at least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-03T13:48:36-07:00","id":1137019,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shawarbaaz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1136212-vampire-vs-mages?p=1137013#post1137013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Versus wise depends on the scenario, a mage could engulf a vampire with fire using the Forces Arcana and call it a day,</div> </div> </div> </div>Here is where Resilence come in. I mean, I'm not saying the vampire is better. I'm just saying that he can stands and it is at par and depending on the build.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-03T15:22:07-07:00","id":1137065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hoodedclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1136212-vampire-vs-mages?p=1137001#post1137001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, I don't see this disparity that is getting so much attention. Yes, if the mage has plenty of time to prepare and everything goes his way and all the arcana fall into place etc; sure. Odd game you are playing, though, where the mage gets to plan a slow hit on the vamp without any plot complications.<br /> <br /> Much is made of the unmaking spells, for instance. Instakill buttons are scary. But to get there, a mage needs a) 5 dots in an arcanum and b) 5 dots in gnosis. A comparable leech is scary as hell. Even before any disciplines are added, a vampire with 5 BP in frenzy can add 15 to any physical dicepool. One sniper bullet out of the mage's sensory range/thrown barstool in range and he is likely toast - even for a vampire with no dots in the relevant abilities. Or 15 dots to sneak up (or merely 10 if you rule the current frenzy supercedes the ability to be a stealthy predator) before adding any natural skills. If you get close enough for the grapple, that +15 dice is v. likely to give you an exceptional success - which means an additional +5 damage due to blood loss if you apply the feed move. Depending on how you take the wording, a 5BP vampire should get an additional +5 to either stamina or all withstand ratings in frenzy. Even an unprepared vampire in a physical confrontation is terrifying, and almost certainly lethal, to most mages if they get within grabbing distance. And this is all before you apply disciplines, ghoul hordes etc.<br /> <br /> Of course, if the mage is sniping from safety, the vampire might die. Vice versa, too, though. If the sniper rifle from a helicopter doesn't take your fancy, how about the level 2 cruac ritual that kills any mortal at any distance by exploding their bowels (Shed the Virulent Bowels, I believe). Or some of the resist magic merits from the same.<br /> <br /> In my mage game? We had one obfuscate 3 vampire tear up two different mages - one with matter 4, one with death 4. We even had the death specialist immune to obfuscate with an improvised spell (the mage won the clash), but stellar stealth rolls meant the vampire got in there and stomped the mage in a grapple. Both mages ended up bloodbound in a cellar - for more drama ensuing. There is a chance in the next game that our acanthus is going to have a battle with some vamp heavy in fortitude, and I think trickiness is going to be more useful than any agg damage.<br /> <br /> Theoretically, sitting in my armchair, I know how to prevent a mugging. When it happens, I hope the muggers work out what I have planned for them, and are glad to go along with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>One vampire beat 2 mages adept mages, one with death 4 who was immune to the obfuscate. Then they werent played properly or really really badly. Death veiling means how did the vampire even spot them? The matter mage should have had at least double digit armor, and if not why not? Why wasnt the death mage made of shadow? Grappling that is hard.<br /> <br /> Yep, they were played really badly my friend. It doesnt take mastery to be scary as mages. Forces 2 negates all bullets, knifes, grapples, via shielding vs kinetic energy. And thats 2 dots.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-03T15:29:59-07:00","id":1137068,"title":"","content":"Also you can cast during a grapple, regardless of whether you win the roll or not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-03T15:32:22-07:00","id":1137071,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1136212-vampire-vs-mages?p=1137068#post1137068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also you can cast during a grapple, regardless of whether you win the roll or not.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think there is a negative three penalty if you lose the grapple. Don't quote me on that, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-03T15:34:08-07:00","id":1137072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ever Professional</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1136212-vampire-vs-mages?p=1137071#post1137071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think there is a negative three penalty if you lose the grapple. Don't quote me on that, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's right. Not all that big in the grand scheme of things. Just a spell factor and a half, and if the vamp's <i>right there...</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-03T15:40:00-07:00","id":1137077,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1136212-vampire-vs-mages?p=1137065#post1137065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Death veiling means how did the vampire even spot them?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's possible they didn't have death veiling up.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The matter mage should have had at least double digit armor, and if not why not?<br /> <br /> Forces 2 negates all bullets, knifes, grapples, via shielding vs kinetic energy. And thats 2 dots. </div> </div> </div>Matter and Forces armor do almost the same thing, providing General Armor based on your Arcana with some side benefits. The Matter Mage would have 4 General Armor if they activated it.<br /> <br /> 'Forces Armor disperses the energy of attacks before they can reach the mage, much like a force field.<br /> Forces Armor applies the mage\u2019s full Forces rating as general armor, applicable against all damaging physical attacks and the automatic damage from fire and electricity. It has no effect on mental or psychic attacks.'<br /> <br /> 'Matter Armor changes the properties of the matter surrounding the mage to protect her; her clothes solidify to repel a fist, a bullet softens to lessen the impact, or ambient moisture condenses to quench a fireball.<br /> Matter Armor applies the mage\u2019s full Matter rating as general armor, applicable against all damaging physical attacks. It is immune to Armor Piercing. Matter Armor has no effect on mental or psychic attacks.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-03T15:51:11-07:00","id":1137083,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1136212-vampire-vs-mages?p=1137077#post1137077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's possible they didn't have death veiling up.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Matter and Forces armor do almost the same thing, providing General Armor based on your Arcana with some side benefits. The Matter Mage would have 4 General Armor if they activated it.<br /> <br /> 'Forces Armor disperses the energy of attacks before they can reach the mage, much like a force field.<br /> Forces Armor applies the mage\u2019s full Forces rating as general armor, applicable against all damaging physical attacks and the automatic damage from fire and electricity. It has no effect on mental or psychic attacks.'<br /> <br /> 'Matter Armor changes the properties of the matter surrounding the mage to protect her; her clothes solidify to repel a fist, a bullet softens to lessen the impact, or ambient moisture condenses to quench a fireball.<br /> Matter Armor applies the mage\u2019s full Matter rating as general armor, applicable against all damaging physical attacks. It is immune to Armor Piercing. Matter Armor has no effect on mental or psychic attacks.'</div> </div> </div> </div>Im talking about forces shielding practice, not mage armor.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">Most commonly with the Practice of Shielding (<span style=\"font-family:Arial-Black\">\u2022\u2022<span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">), a spell may grant protection from forces under the Arcanum\u2019s purview.<br /> These spells usually provide blanket immunity to natural or mundane phenomena</span></span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>its a common mistake, but creative thaum makes it possible to get blanket protection from kinetic force.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-03T15:54:13-07:00","id":1137084,"title":"","content":"General purpose magical defense is handled by Mage Armor, not a spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-03T15:57:08-07:00","id":1137086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1136212-vampire-vs-mages?p=1137083#post1137083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">its a common mistake, but creative thaum makes it possible to get blanket protection from kinetic force.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is a common mistake. You can look at Alchemist's Touch's touch example and see that you would only get protection equal to your Potency, depending on how much Reach you used.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-03T15:59:47-07:00","id":1137089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1136212-vampire-vs-mages?p=1137065#post1137065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then they werent played properly or really really badly. Death veiling means how did the vampire even spot them? <br /> <br /> Yep, they were played really badly my friend.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the advice. Not seeing the threat, or knowing everything about its capabilities, did have something to do with the effectiveness of their preparations. But I'll pass on to my players your judgement of their mettle!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/668-hoodedclaw","name":"hoodedclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-03T16:06:01-07:00","id":1137094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1136212-vampire-vs-mages?p=1136310#post1136310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Following scenario:<br /> A Kindred with his teeth in the Organized Crime Scene controls a majority of people via powerful blood bonds, use of Majesty and let's throw in the occasional Dominate. So let us assume a Coils of the Voivode 4, Majesty 4, Dominate 3 kinda guy.<br /> For unspecified reasons, a non-Mind Mage (Let's go with a Time 4/Fate 3/Life 2/Space 2 Acanthus) needs to wrestle that control away. (He needs the Control to end, not necessarily the vamp, nor does he merely need some gangsters to do something for him).<br /> In this scenario, for some reason, both cannot rely on their Cabal/Coterie as those are busy otherwise, vanilla mortals are fair game though.<br /> <br /> A) both know of each other, and their respective goals<br /> B) neither knows about the supernatural nature of the other (yet) but are aware of each other's existance (There's this guy that wants my power gone/I need to remove that guy's control)<br /> C) neither know anything about the other<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Being aware of the the existence means being able to scry it, not knowing name and weak link will require time (boom boom time 4) but once thats possible, mage sight will ping alerting the mage to the kindreds supernatural nature, time/life can probably be used remotely to determine its dead/a vampire.<br /> <br /> A remote casting of shared fate + grave misfortune will mean the next time the vampire feeds from a mortal and does 1 lethal from blood loss he'll take 1 + grave misfortunes potency (base 3) lethal damage. Once the vampire torpors himself, he'll be easy to abuse with sympathetic magic as killing him seems the best way to break his hold on people right?<br /> <br /> Worst case scenario is temporal stutter the vampire and any lackeys lucky to be near him into the future remotely, for an indefinate duration and release the spell, he's gone till some dispels it. Defenses might include a hung temporal pocket, triggered to go of when surprised, sending him into safety the moment somebody surprises him, unlikely with time though.<br /> <br /> This is all from the safety of the mage's sanctum mind, he probably hasnt got dressed yet either..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-03T16:11:18-07:00","id":1137098,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1136212-vampire-vs-mages?p=1137086#post1137086\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It is a common mistake. You can look at Alchemist's Touch's touch example and see that you would only get protection equal to your Potency, depending on how much Reach you used.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Actually no, there is nothing under creative thaum that requires that and basing it of alchemists touch isnt needed. All creative thaum says is protects vs supernatural attacks equal to the the potency, and such attacks clash. But then the actual examples of shielding spells, dont have that either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-03T16:13:27-07:00","id":1137099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1136212-vampire-vs-mages?p=1137094#post1137094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Being aware of the the existence means being able to scry it, not knowing name and weak link will require time (boom boom time 4) but once thats possible, mage sight will ping alerting the mage to the kindreds supernatural nature, time/life can probably be used remotely to determine its dead/a vampire.<br /> <br /> A remote casting of shared fate + grave misfortune will mean the next time the vampire feeds from a mortal and does 1 lethal from blood loss he'll take 1 + grave misfortunes potency (base 3) lethal damage. Once the vampire torpors himself, he'll be easy to abuse with sympathetic magic as killing him seems the best way to break his hold on people right?<br /> <br /> Worst case scenario is temporal stutter the vampire and any lackeys lucky to be near him into the future remotely, for an indefinate duration and release the spell, he's gone till some dispels it. Defenses might include a hung temporal pocket, triggered to go of when surprised, sending him into safety the moment somebody surprises him, unlikely with time though.<br /> <br /> This is all from the safety of the mage's sanctum mind, he probably hasnt got dressed yet either..</div> </div> </div> </div>That requires a lot of arcana. Like, a lot. I could see a Cabal pulling that off, but I kind of doubt a single mage could. It also raises the question of why. Like, why would these two be fighting? And why would a mage's first response be &quot;I must absolutely murder the hell out of the vampire&quot;?<br /> <br /> On that note, why is the vampire targeting the mage? I mean, sure they could have some issues against each other. But the mage is a mortal, so why would the vampire raise the stakes to murdering said mage? The vampire will probably outlive the mage.<br /> <br /> And if the mage is just tossing spells around to murder people, they might get a visit from other mages who don't think that's okay to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-03T16:14:24-07:00","id":1137101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1136212-vampire-vs-mages?p=1137084#post1137084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">General purpose magical defense is handled by Mage Armor, not a spell.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Go read the shielding practice, and learn about shielding spells, shielding is used to protect against stuff too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-03T16:15:27-07:00","id":1137103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ever Professional</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1136212-vampire-vs-mages?p=1137099#post1137099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That requires a lot of arcana. Like, a lot. I could see a Cabal pulling that off, but I kind of doubt a single mage could. It also raises the question of why. Like, why would these two be fighting? And why would a mage's first response be &quot;I must absolutely murder the hell out of the vampire&quot;?<br /> <br /> On that note, why is the vampire targeting the mage? I mean, sure they could have some issues against each other. But the mage is a mortal, so why would the vampire raise the stakes to murdering said mage? The vampire will probably outlive the mage.<br /> <br /> And if the mage is just tossing spells around to murder people, they might get a visit from other mages who don't think that's okay to do.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> NO it requires the arcana he said the mage had, time 4, fate 3, life sommat and space 2. I was working with what he gave me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-03T16:17:18-07:00","id":1137105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ever Professional</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1136212-vampire-vs-mages?p=1137099#post1137099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That requires a lot of arcana. Like, a lot. I could see a Cabal pulling that off, but I kind of doubt a single mage could. It also raises the question of why. Like, why would these two be fighting? And why would a mage's first response be &quot;I must absolutely murder the hell out of the vampire&quot;?<br /> <br /> On that note, why is the vampire targeting the mage? I mean, sure they could have some issues against each other. But the mage is a mortal, so why would the vampire raise the stakes to murdering said mage? The vampire will probably outlive the mage.<br /> <br /> And if the mage is just tossing spells around to murder people, they might get a visit from other mages who don't think that's okay to do.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Vampires arnt people <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> This particular vampire seems to have alot of people as slaves, so ending its existance is probably for the betterment of mankind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-03T16:24:00-07:00","id":1137108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1136212-vampire-vs-mages?p=1137105#post1137105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Vampires arnt people <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> This particular vampire seems to have alot of people as slaves, so ending its existance is probably for the betterment of mankind.</div> </div> </div> </div>But why would they think that? I mean, vampires have souls and stuff, and I thought to be counted as person you needed a soul. And while that mage might not consider vampires people, other mages might.<br /> <br /> And isn't the mage pretty much going to do the whole slave thing to? It is a useful method. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-03T16:24:56-07:00","id":1137109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1136212-vampire-vs-mages?p=1137103#post1137103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> NO it requires the arcana he said the mage had, time 4, fate 3, life sommat and space 2. I was working with what he gave me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair, but my point still stands. That is a lot of arcana, and I don't see why they would go straight to murdering when a joint business seems more profitable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-03T16:26:44-07:00","id":1137111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1136212-vampire-vs-mages?p=1137094#post1137094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> BA remote casting of shared fate + grave misfortune will mean the next time the vampire feeds from a mortal and does 1 lethal from blood loss he'll take 1 + grave misfortunes potency (base 3) lethal damage. Once the vampire torpors himself, he'll be easy to abuse with sympathetic magic as killing him seems the best way to break his hold on people right?<br /> <br /> Worst case scenario is temporal stutter the vampire and any lackeys lucky to be near him into the future remotely, for an indefinate duration and release the spell, he's gone till some dispels it. Defenses might include a hung temporal pocket, triggered to go of when surprised, sending him into safety the moment somebody surprises him, unlikely with time though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like your st plays fast and loose with paradox rules, and gives you a lot of the information you need to devise the perfect solution to every problem. More power to you! It is one style of gaming.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/668-hoodedclaw","name":"hoodedclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-03T16:28:32-07:00","id":1137112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ever Professional</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1136212-vampire-vs-mages?p=1137109#post1137109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Fair, but my point still stands. That is a lot of arcana, and I don't see why they would go straight to murdering when a joint business seems more profitable.</div> </div> </div> </div>So yeh, without mind he probably isnt going anywhere near a vampire who can command people and gets them to drink his blood and then become his slave. Remember he has seen the things past/future along with his own, he'll know what the best outcome should be <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. A simple time spell will tell you its probably not a good idea to try get into bed with this thing without serious mind shields or something..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-03T16:33:46-07:00","id":1137113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hoodedclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1136212-vampire-vs-mages?p=1137111#post1137111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sounds like your st plays fast and loose with paradox rules, and gives you a lot of the information you need to devise the perfect solution to every problem. More power to you! It is one style of gaming.</div> </div> </div> </div>Paradox is managable if kept away from sleepers, and there are things known as demenses that make it a non issue, he didnt mention one but even without one there is little over reaching involved that cant be managed with mana expendature and eating as a nose bleed or two.<br /> <br /> ST doesnt have to give any information its called being experienced with mages abilities, it is probably standard practice to scry something using space, use time to view its past/future, if a mage isnt doing these things to something it knows nothing about, then he deserves to get whacked.<br /> <br /> Take your example earlier it clearly shows your players are new and maybe dont understand what they can do or what they should do. Its not that much effort for a mage with matter 4 to make +10 or more armour clothes for his entire cabal, then release the spell. He can give his entire cabal a +10 armour set of jeans + tshirt using matter. Why wouldnt he do it?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 09-03-2017, 07:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-03T16:35:56-07:00","id":1137115,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1136212-vampire-vs-mages?p=1137112#post1137112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So yeh, without mind he probably isnt going anywhere near a vampire who can command people and gets them to drink his blood and then become his slave. Remember he has seen the things past/future along with his own, he'll know what the best outcome should be <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. A simple time spell will tell you its probably not a good idea to try get into bed with this thing without serious mind shields or something..</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, doesn't Time pretty much state the future isn't set in stone, and the future could very well be changing by mere virtue of you having forseen what might come?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-03T16:45:33-07:00","id":1137118,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ever Professional</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1136212-vampire-vs-mages?p=1137115#post1137115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, doesn't Time pretty much state the future isn't set in stone, and the future could very well be changing by mere virtue of you having forseen what might come?</div> </div> </div> </div>To an extent but if that was the case then scrying the future would be useless wouldnt it?, simply asking &quot;Will anything bad/harmful happen to me or my friends/loved ones if i were to try deal with X in a civil manner?&quot; (Im sure you could word this better too but its an example) and if the answer came back &quot;Yes&quot; then you know trying to be civil isnt going to work <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-03T16:52:19-07:00","id":1137122,"title":"","content":"This is why white room scenarios dont work though, to many opinions and such. Somebody gets accused of being to lenient or having to much fore knowledge. In any white room how much prep time does the mage get? Does the player know what he will be up against (a vampire in this case) so he can choose whatever? Are both splats just plopped into a room with xyz and told to duke it out. Does the vampire get to start obfuscated? How much exp do they both get, are they just starting characters? Blah blah blah, you really have to nail everything down and frankly whatever the outcome one side will cry and probably declare it a fluke or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 09-03-2017, 07:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-03T17:06:27-07:00","id":1137125,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1136212-vampire-vs-mages?p=1137098#post1137098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually no, there is nothing under creative thaum that requires that and basing it of alchemists touch isnt needed.</div> </div> </div> </div>The existing spells suggest what creative magics might be and how they would be formed. If Alchemist's Touch could offer complete blanket to all harmful effects, there would be no need to have a line saying it only protects up to Potency.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> All creative thaum says is protects vs supernatural attacks equal to the the potency, and such attacks clash. But then the actual examples of shielding spells, dont have that either. </div> </div> </div>Most of the other examples aren't things that can be used as weapons against you, for instance through Time and Space. Matter stands out likely because many supernatural attacks are going to be Matter-based, especially since the lines build off of one another.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1136212-vampire-vs-mages?p=1137122#post1137122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is why white room scenarios dont work though, to many opinions and such. Somebody gets accused of being to lenient or having to much fore knowledge... Blah blah blah, you really have to nail everything down and frankly whatever the outcome one side will cry and probably declare it a fluke or something.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is literally what you did to hoodedclaw.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1136212-vampire-vs-mages?p=1136325#post1136325\">It's also why Marcus put forth the idea of having two characters of equivalent stats to face off against each other.</a> And why, since the beginning, people have been suggesting to avoid the nonsense-ridden white room of 'but this character would always do that.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-03-2017, 08:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-03T17:11:16-07:00","id":1137127,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1136212-vampire-vs-mages?p=1137125#post1137125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The existing spells suggest what creative magics might be and how they would be formed. If Alchemist's Touch could offer complete blanket to all harmful effects, there would be no need to have a line saying it only protects up to Potency.</div> </div> </div> </div>Look at the Reach effects for Alchemist's Touch. For a Force analog, tt can easily render a mage totally immune to all bashing and lethal kinetic damage, and Potency reduction against aggravated damaged (and with each additional Reach, add another type of force like fire and heat, electricity, radiation, etc.).<br /> <br /> Absent some clarification from Dave, Forces 2 Shielding seems really badass against non-mage foes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-03T17:17:00-07:00","id":1137130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1136212-vampire-vs-mages?p=1137127#post1137127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Look at the Reach effects for Alchemist's Touch. For a Force analog, tt can easily render a mage totally immune to all bashing and lethal kinetic damage, and Potency reduction against aggravated damaged (and with each additional Reach, add another type of force like fire and heat, electricity, radiation, etc.).</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, but first, you look at my post <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1136212-vampire-vs-mages?p=1137086#post1137086\">here</a>, where I brought that up. Unless your character has Infinite Potency, he is not immune to damage.<br /> <br /> Then you might ask hoodedclaw how the vampire did damage, if you wanted to post on topic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-03T17:45:21-07:00","id":1137136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1136212-vampire-vs-mages?p=1137125#post1137125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The existing spells suggest what creative magics might be and how they would be formed. If Alchemist's Touch could offer complete blanket to all harmful effects, there would be no need to have a line saying it only protects up to Potency.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Most of the other examples aren't things that can be used as weapons against you, for instance through Time and Space. Matter stands out likely because many supernatural attacks are going to be Matter-based, especially since the lines build off of one another.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> That is literally what you did to hoodedclaw.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1136212-vampire-vs-mages?p=1136325#post1136325\">It's also why Marcus put forth the idea of having two characters of equivalent stats to face off against each other.</a> And why, since the beginning, people have been suggesting to avoid the nonsense-ridden white room of 'but this character would always do that.'</div> </div> </div> </div>Well for one, you are already arguing about using forces 2 to neuter vampires physical attacks. There is no equivalence when it comes to disciples vs arcana though. One Arcana at 4 can cover multiple things a discipline can do or even more than one. Take mind 4, it can cover Auspex telepathy, Dominate, Majesty, Obfuscate, Nightmare and probably others.<br /> <br /> A starting mage with forces 3 and prime 2 and mind 1 gets a kinetic shield, kinetic blow, supernal veil or invisibility right off the bat and then control fire along with mind unveiling which should give a clash vs obfuscate..What does a vampire get? 3 dots in disciplines? Which seems to be obfuscate 3 from most of the talk so far. <br /> <br /> If you allow the vampire to start obfuscated, you have to allow the mage to start invis or supernal veiled and the vampire doesnt have auspex right? Etc etc on and on...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-04T02:17:33-07:00","id":1137246,"title":"","content":"Yes - these tit for tat firebacks - &quot;but the mage could have had this/vampire this&quot; do assume OOC knowledge the character (and player) may not have. I do not want to get into a weird &quot;I quote you this, now you counter my logic&quot; argument about what could go down theoretically, but will give a bit more insight into the Obfuscate 3 vamp taking down two mages.<br /> <br /> The mages were trying to protect one of their children who had come home from a weekend with their father bloodbound. So the matter mage turned the house into a safe haven (improvised matter 4 spell); also rose a golem; both mages put on enhanced senses with life, the death mage went shadow form and also a death sheilding spell on both (won the clash of wills vs obfuscate). As paradox ramps quickly in combat - in our experience/playstyle - they didn't load on more protection, to leave some room for damage spells.<br /> <br /> Two ghouls attacked the house to &quot;rescue&quot; the kid. Yes, the mages quashed them - fairly quickly, if I recall - but garnered some pdox. But then - in the lull afterwards (and as they both failed to penetrate the boosted stealth rolls of the mekhet, even though one of them was rolling 11 dice) they started the clean-up. Matter mage goes up to sooth the kid - only just awoke; death mage reforms to dispose of the bodies/deal with the cops after gunfire outside the house. Then the Mekhet cannot withold frenzy any more from the shadows, pops out and flattens the death mage, then goes up to do the same to the matter mage.<br /> <br /> I twisted the rules a bit. The death mage should have been dead, but I allowed them both to wake up afterwards, bloodbound in a cellar on a vitae drip, being served water by the child. <br /> <br /> Yes, I am sure this is playing badly by some standards - but it was a great fun and dramatic session. Sorry if we are playing it wrong. But the mages were prepped - for vampires. And although on the page we could argue &quot;but I can counter this with that&quot; - the way it worked out in play was very different. And mad craic. <br /> <br /> If the players had all the knowledge - when and who and how many and from what direction and at what time etc - they could beat anything. But even as I start to incorporate time magic into my chronicle - with divination - it is limited by potency, gameplay and knowledge of the targets (as the acanthus can only foresee the future of things he can target; so himself is valid, but &quot;my enemies&quot; is partial at best). <br /> <br /> Anyhow - work beckons. But I think a lot of the arguing on behalf of mages assumes a god's eye view. Which is perhaps the strength of mages, and armchair theorising, but is not always absolute in gameplay, even with time magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/668-hoodedclaw","name":"hoodedclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-04T06:11:16-07:00","id":1137273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hoodedclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1136212-vampire-vs-mages?p=1137246#post1137246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Snippy snip.</div> </div> </div> </div>So reforming from shadow flesh was a big mistake right? He could still have dealt with the bodies while in shadow flesh form via things like corpse mask or whatever, i mean invisibility in darkness and being able to see in them while being virtually immune to physical damage, you dont leave that until you are sure things are over.<br /> <br /> Plus are you aware that ghouls count as sleepwalkers so dont trigger paradox dice, if they were over reaching in combat thats fine though.<br /> <br /> But yeh you were all having fun and that is what it is all about, I was the ST for a 1e game for 3ish years so maybe im just jaded because I was the won constantly having to say &quot;Er, Nope.&quot; or &quot;how does that work?&quot; to my players, who really pushed the boat out for super lethal stupid stuff. Its been ages since they were new to mage, im sure most new mages (&amp; new players) make mistakes and end up dead its good to thin the herd i suppose.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-04T07:01:28-07:00","id":1137280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1136212-vampire-vs-mages?p=1137101#post1137101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Go read the shielding practice, and learn about shielding spells, shielding is used to protect against stuff too.</div> </div> </div> </div>I did. It specifically doesn't cover general purpose stuff like &quot;immunity to all attacks.&quot;<br /> <br /> For a forum setting, also, you need to not count Creative Thaumaturgy. While it is a core part of Mage, the effectiveness of it is going to be too different from table to table.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1157,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","user":"SoulGambit","date":". 09-04-2017, 10:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-04T07:40:10-07:00","id":1137292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1136212-vampire-vs-mages?p=1137280#post1137280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I did. It specifically doesn't cover general purpose stuff like &quot;immunity to all attacks.&quot;<br /> <br /> For a forum setting, also, you need to not count Creative Thaumaturgy. While it is a core part of Mage, the effectiveness of it is going to be too different from table to table.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> What part of &quot;blanket immunity&quot; did you miss? Nobody has said immunity to all attacks, but a shield providing blanket immunity from kinetic energy, will cover: Bullets, fists, knifes, grapples, etc etc, any other mundane expression of kinetic energy used in an attack it would not cover certain magical attacks and mental/psychic attacks though.<br /> <br /> If you create a shielding spell vs fire with forces 2, you will be totally immune to mundane fire, and supernatural fire will need to win clashes and protect for a number of attacks up to potency.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 09-04-2017, 10:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-04T07:50:37-07:00","id":1137298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1136212-vampire-vs-mages?p=1137273#post1137273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So reforming from shadow flesh was a big mistake right? He could still have dealt with the bodies while in shadow flesh form via things like corpse mask or whatever, i mean invisibility in darkness and being able to see in them while being virtually immune to physical damage, you dont leave that until you are sure things are over.<br /> <br /> Plus are you aware that ghouls count as sleepwalkers so dont trigger paradox dice, if they were over reaching in combat thats fine though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, the mages were quite sure the situation was dealt with, and could not sense anything about, trusting their enhanced senses. And no, the ghouls did not add any pdox dice.<br /> <br /> I think I might resolve Creative Thaumaturgy a bit more rigidly than you; not dealt with forces magic much, but would be a touch wary of granting immunity to all kinetic damage without some provisos/reach/relevance of spell potency. Also some of the other spells you mention would not be as unproblematic at my table - armoured clothes relinquished indefinitely would bring in some dissonance and go awry eventually at my table. But more power to you if the style works.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/668-hoodedclaw","name":"hoodedclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-04T08:02:13-07:00","id":1137307,"title":"","content":"I think totalgit is indeed overestimating the power of shielding spells.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-04T08:47:57-07:00","id":1137320,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hoodedclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1136212-vampire-vs-mages?p=1137298#post1137298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh, the mages were quite sure the situation was dealt with, and could not sense anything about, trusting their enhanced senses. And no, the ghouls did not add any pdox dice.<br /> <br /> I think I might resolve Creative Thaumaturgy a bit more rigidly than you; not dealt with forces magic much, but would be a touch wary of granting immunity to all kinetic damage without some provisos/reach/relevance of spell potency. Also some of the other spells you mention would not be as unproblematic at my table - armoured clothes relinquished indefinitely would bring in some dissonance and go awry eventually at my table. But more power to you if the style works.</div> </div> </div> </div>You seem under the impression that i ignore the drawbacks for mages or something, or that i let my players off easily? Dissonance is a problem, your spell will go awry eventually but my players would rather survive that tank shell and worry about it later than not survive the tank shell? It happens at the end of a scene and needs folk to get 4+ successes on a integrity roll? And lowers the armor by 1 for each success over it, so would need to get alot of successes before it lowered it to a unreasonable level, duration would only vanish once the potency factors have been eroded. Maybe you are still just unfamilar with stuff and think that its a bigger deal than it ends up being.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3166_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3166\" data-vbnamecard=\"3166\">Elfive</a> Remember the reason the printed shielding spells mention clashes etc is that its assuming that they are being hit with supernatural sources etc, shielding as written makes mundane sources of things trivial. Constant presence is shielding vs time, it renders you completely immune to time so you no longer age and im the one overestimating the power of shielding spells? Nope, most people underestimate them greatly, esp vs the mundane. Look at enviromental shield, makes you completely immune to conditions/tilts caused by enviroments, how is that not blanket protection? <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-04T09:18:47-07:00","id":1137332,"title":"","content":"I don't think vampires count as an extreme environment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-04T11:41:49-07:00","id":1137380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1136212-vampire-vs-mages?p=1137320#post1137320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You seem under the impression that i ignore the drawbacks for mages or something, or that i let my players off easily? </div> </div> </div> </div>I do have that impression yes - but not just of you; of many mage players who compare them in white-room style situations on the forums. But it seems quite a popular playstyle - if it doesn't match my reading of the game - so if it works for you, go for it! I would say that many of the printed spells in 2E often have all kinds of complications to them to get the utmost benefit - such as requiring multiple reach for high/versatile benefits - and this is the philosophy I try to aim for at the table. Paradox has never been entirely negligible in my games- it is a regular threat in every combat scene. Protective magic takes up spell slots, and then consecutive spells ramp paradox quickly - particularly with multiple &quot;waves&quot; of sustained threats. But it sounds like you are enjoying it too - so whatever works for you and your group!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/668-hoodedclaw","name":"hoodedclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-04T12:22:07-07:00","id":1137395,"title":"","content":"The issue with custom mechanics is that Vampires have custom devotions, then it's all pointless.<br /> <br /> Let's look at the Arcana and see what problem powers Mages have, and let's restrict things to creation traits for now. I will include a CT note on &quot;things this arcana can probably do&quot; to aknowledge them, but not otherwise consider them.<br /> <br /> DEATH<br /> - Level 1: There isn't much here, but Focused Mage Sight (Death) allows the Mage to scrutinize Vampires. If a Vampire is leaving corpses/ghosts, then they are leaving tractable clues.<br /> - Level 2: Nothing of note. The Mage can hide their trace.<br /> - Level 3: Direct Damage comes in here. They also get a gtfo via Twilight. Most importantly, they get tons of Ghostly and Zombie minions.<br /> - CT: Level 2 can probably CoW against most Kindred Powers and Invisibility vs them. Can empower zombies as well as ghosts at 3.<br /> <br /> FATE<br /> - Level 1: Some nice dice adders if the Mage isn't rushed and the ability to make good decisions / find Vampires. Can also automatically detect supernatural mind control.<br /> - Level 2: You get the all powerful Exceptional Luck, which imo should be a Rote on almost every mage. An Apprentice of Fate also has as many social merits as they want, and those merits are expendable. Can Shield against all Aoe and Mind Control on the same spell. Fools Rush In is one of the best dice adder in the game.<br /> - Level 3: Rote on Tap, some nice debuffs. Monkey's Paw is a no-Withstand curse.<br /> <br /> FORCES<br /> - Level 1: The ability to tune in on internet/cellphone/etc is not to be underestimated.<br /> - Level 2: Control Fire is always solid. Invisibility is here, as is Zoom In, part of a &quot;witness everything&quot; combo. Transmission is not to be underestimated.<br /> - Level 3: Call Lightning is a two hit kill against most things. Various telekinesis style powers are here.<br /> - CT: Can probably illusion cameras, etc to falsify evidence and frame the Kindred.<br /> <br /> LIFE<br /> - Level 1: Perception boosts are nice.<br /> - Level 2: Lure/Repel is a good social (de)buff. Control Instincts has a lot of good uses. <br /> - Level 3: Damage and Defrading the Form probably won't work on vampires. That said, the Mage gets Attribute Buffs and Animal Mods and Healing.<br /> <br /> MATTER<br /> - Level 1: Can't suffocate a Vampire to death, thankfully. Can get 8-again on rolls to use something, or skip the roll all together and get straight successes when operating a device. Probably lowest hanging autostake fruit.<br /> - Level 2: Not too much here. Illusioning cameras is nice. Shaping can make instant pits or even trap someone depending on how the ST rules it.<br /> - Level 3: Alter Conductivity can melt neighborhoods into slag or kill everyone in it. Shrink/Grow has some interesting uses. State Change can make solid air prisons with no Withstand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1157,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","user":"SoulGambit","date":". 09-04-2017, 03:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-04T12:45:17-07:00","id":1137407,"title":"","content":"MIND<br /> - Level 1: Lots of good information-gathering powers here. Knowing nature, goals, surface emotions, etc. It's Auspex 1-2. Mage Sight can pick out Mind Control.<br /> - Level 2: Powerful social buffs to build and exploit trust. You also get Dominate 1-2 and Auspex 4. Can Shield against mental powers. You also get all of Obfuscate, basically.<br /> - Level 3: Attribute / Skill buffs. Can summon and control Goetia (Emphemeral). Instant sleep powers are combat enders. You get deep mind reading and memory alteration.<br /> <br /> PRIME <br /> - Level 1: Discern Truth is how Mages pierce obfuscate and find shapeshifted Vampires. It also perfectly detect lies, which completely changes the social game. Supernal Vision lets them pick vampires out of the crowd.<br /> - Level 2: Cloak Mage nature from, e.g. Auspex.<br /> - Level 3: Platonic Form is good general utility.<br /> <br /> SPACE<br /> - Level 1: Correspondance can get a LOT of information gathering. Isolation can shut down a Kindred's ability to feed. Locate Object is a way to find and track vampires. The Outward and Inward Eye is Bashit nuts insane. Combine with Zoom In for fun.<br /> - Level 2: Scry and Die comes in to play. Breaking Bonds makes it near impossible to incarcerate the Mage. Lying Maps can keep a Kindred running through the streets at noon instead of finding safety. <br /> - Level 3: Can just Ban a Vampire until they hit Torpor with nothing to do. Teleportation, even reflexive hit and run teleport is possible. <br /> <br /> SPIRIT<br /> - Level 1: Nothing too dangerous here. Not a lot of intersection between vamps and spirits.<br /> - Level 2: All kinds of uses for Command Spirit. <br /> - Level 3: Spirit minions, go! So many uses for this.<br /> <br /> TIME<br /> - Level 1: This is The Problem information gathering wise. Postcognition and Divination means that the Mage knows the vampire is coming and can investigate what the vampire was doing. <br /> - Level 2: Veil of Moments protects against conditions in general.<br /> - Level 3: Acceleration is a great Dodge booster, allows for interrupt actions. Temporal Summoning is effectively a one cast disable that for some reason doesn't have Withstand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1157,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","user":"SoulGambit","date":". 09-04-2017, 03:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-04T13:15:48-07:00","id":1137424,"title":"","content":"Let's start with a Social Mage. You want Fate 2 on a social Mage for the free merits and Prime 1 for Discern Truth, period. After that you want Mind, Life, or Forces 2. Time 1 for divination/postcognition is probably the best single dot bang for buck arcana from there if we have the luxury.<br /> <br /> Acanthus with Fate 2, Time 1, Prime 1, Mind or Life 2<br /> Mastigos with Mind 2, Space 1, Fate 2, Prime 1<br /> Obrimos with Forces 2, Fate 2, Prime 1, Time 1<br /> Thyrsus with Life 2, Spirit 1, Fate 2, Prime 1<br /> Moros with Death 3, Matter 1, Fate 2<br /> <br /> Nixing Prime for Mind 3 or Forces 3 is a solid option. Exceptional Luck would be a Rote on all of them. I also recommend either Shifting the Odds / Fools Rush In as Rites or doing something like a high Shadow Name.<br /> <br /> Any Mage Specific merits that should be considered? Destiny is ever present and ever op.<br /> <br /> P.s. I don't remember all of the opposing arcana off the top so if I made one if the paths start with it, sorry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1157,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","user":"SoulGambit","date":". 09-04-2017, 04:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-04T14:46:58-07:00","id":1137457,"title":"","content":"So lets set some broad goals.<br /> <br /> Challenge #1: Convince [Target] to allow access to [Item or Location] when it is their job not to.<br /> <br /> Challenge #2: Gain an ally and business partner in a venture. It is in their mutual best interests, but they specifically do not trust you. Hostile starting impressions. Get the best deal.<br /> <br /> Challenge #3: A cop or FBI agent has a personal vendetta against you and a small cell of people willing to listen. This either is or is about to be a Hunter Cell with their sights on you. Convince them to drop the case without alerting the broader authorities further.<br /> <br /> Challenge #4: A small group of mortals have Seen Too Much. Take care of them. Bonus round: how could you handle larger scale Masquerade Breaches?<br /> <br /> Challenge #5: You want to apply social pressure to destroy a rival's assets out of petty revenge. How do you do it?<br /> <br /> For each of those, how do you deal with a Vampire opposing you or doing those things to you?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-04T15:30:59-07:00","id":1137477,"title":"","content":"i thought about it, and probably the OP and other people who might be interested in crossovers will find this topic useful for the purpose of vampires vs mages...<br /> actual game and fight between vampires and mages<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/910711-cabal-at-war-the-power-of-mages-report-from-the-last-game-session/page3\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/910711-cabal-at-war-the-power-of-mages-report-from-the-last-game-session/page3\"> Cabal at war, the power of mages- report from the last game session - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/910711-cabal-at-war-the-power-of-mages-report-from-the-last-game-session/page3\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/910711-cabal-at-war-the-power-of-mages-report-from-the-last-game-session/page3 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> The power of a cabal This is a small recap of last night session with my nerdy friends, and some considerations on what we experienced. Keep in mind that we </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> keep in mind that on that particular case, wizards had all the time to prepare and vampires were almost caught by surprise... but still, it can demonstrate how dangerous mages can be if they decide to go to war.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4247-lasombra","name":"Lasombra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-04T16:53:43-07:00","id":1137506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1136212-vampire-vs-mages?p=1137424#post1137424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let's start with a Social Mage. You want Fate 2 on a social Mage for the free merits and Prime 1 for Discern Truth, period. After that you want Mind, Life, or Forces 2. Time 1 for divination/postcognition is probably the best single dot bang for buck arcana from there if we have the luxury.<br /> <br /> Acanthus with Fate 2, Time 1, Prime 1, Mind or Life 2<br /> Mastigos with Mind 2, Space 1, Fate 2, Prime 1<br /> Obrimos with Forces 2, Fate 2, Prime 1, Time 1<br /> Thyrsus with Life 2, Spirit 1, Fate 2, Prime 1<br /> Moros with Death 3, Matter 1, Fate 2<br /> <br /> Nixing Prime for Mind 3 or Forces 3 is a solid option. Exceptional Luck would be a Rote on all of them. I also recommend either Shifting the Odds / Fools Rush In as Rites or doing something like a high Shadow Name.<br /> <br /> Any Mage Specific merits that should be considered? Destiny is ever present and ever op.<br /> <br /> P.s. I don't remember all of the opposing arcana off the top so if I made one if the paths start with it, sorry.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> This kind of emphasizes the reason why I don't like the mindset that goes into these sort of threads.<br /> <br /> People take character building from a really meta perspective.<br /> <br /> A mage isn't going to go &quot;well, I want some better merits, so I better become an Acanthus and learn Fate 2 before doing anything else.&quot;<br /> <br /> They're going to find an arcana that fits their interests and passions and study it.<br /> <br /> They don't think &quot;Well, obscure fighting style #27 gives me 9-again on fighting with chopsticks, so...&quot; they go pick an art based on their needs and wants, like a self-defense class if that's what they need, or a more authentic martial art if they're interested in the culture and tradition or whatever.<br /> <br /> This is the concept of white-room being applied to character building itself. If you have people min-maxing and trying to build the perfect combat monster of any splat, it's easy as hell to break the Storyteller system. People interested in that are probably better served playing other games. CofD just isn't balanced for that kind of play.<br /> <br /> I'm not trying to say &quot;you're having fun wrong&quot; here so much as &quot;you might have more fun playing something else, if this is what you enjoy&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-04T17:18:00-07:00","id":1137511,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1692_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1692\" data-vbnamecard=\"1692\">Maina</a> Assuming that Magic and the abilities of magic is widespread and Mages know that Fate can spawn important resources and allies essentially from thin air it does, in fact, make sense for engage who wants to leverage magic to gain allies/resources/etc would pursue that Magic in character.<br /> <br /> If I, out of character, want to play a serendipitous Mage who is friend to everyone via magic then I will pick the Magic that does it.<br /> <br /> It only takes on a meta feel in this thread because we are doing a bunch of characters and only fleshing them out just enough to serve our purposes. In a real game we would take those same numbers and flesh out a character and it wouldn't feel meta at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1157,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","user":"SoulGambit","date":". 09-04-2017, 08:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-05T15:22:07-07:00","id":1137849,"title":"","content":"I think I've found the answer to the question of &quot;X vs Y&quot; and the answer is simply &quot;which ever splat the players are using&quot;<br /> <br /> I'm planning to pit my players against a mage manipulating everything in the city to the point of pulling the town into it's own pocket dimension, and I'm betting dollars to donuts the vampires will win somehow, because they're my players and I want them to have fun.<br /> <br /> sorry that I sound rather fun-police-y but that's really just how I see things.<br /> <br /> Also if one is playing a multi-splat game and somehow the players are now fighting each other so that is the context of a 'X vs Y&quot; debate I feel the need to ask how the gm allowed that to occur<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12235-emmens","name":"emmens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12235_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-05T16:18:28-07:00","id":1137860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>emmens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1136212-vampire-vs-mages?p=1137849#post1137849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Also if one is playing a multi-splat game and somehow the players are now fighting each other so that is the context of a 'X vs Y&quot; debate I feel the need to ask how the gm allowed that to occur</div> </div> </div> </div>'Cause it's a horror game and mistrust and betrayal can be well-used themes with a good group. Not every party is composed of True Companions. Sometimes its an alliance of convenience.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-06T08:08:32-07:00","id":1138019,"title":"","content":"Mortal Challenges<br /> #1: Sympathetic + Fast-Talking 4 + a decent persuasion/subterfuge roll should be able to get in.<br /> #2 Need to do some Investigating to learn the subject's vice and use it to boost impressions. Then as above.<br /> #3 Here the mortal struggles. Blackmail and forcing doors are immediate options, but very dangerous.<br /> #4 Really got nothing but coming alongside to support or intimidation or murder.<br /> #5 Need some relevant Allies or Status or use social rolls / blackmail on the group directly.<br /> <br /> Mage<br /> #1 Any can whip up Allies [that security company] if they have time and use Fools Rush In for better social rolls. Mind can Dominate the security or emotional urge them away or Incognito Presence to get the thing. Life can either control instincts, lure/Repel the social system, or force an unfortunately tomes bowl movement. Forces 2+ can just use invisibility or take an alarm elsewhere, while shutting off any electronic alarms. Death 3, Mind 3, Spirit 3 can send in an ephemeral entity.<br /> #2 Fools Rush In boosts impressions to a usable level, as does Lure/Repel and that Mind Spell. In this case you want to use Magic to buff your mundane rolls because if you use magic to get this ally that takes up a control slot. <br /> #3 Killing him would be easy, but may attract suspicion. You are back to acting like a mortal with (significant!) Buffs unless you want to tie up control slots.<br /> #4 So, memory alteration doesn't come in until Mind 3, and even then it isnt lasting. Time 3 could rewind the offending scene. You are better off discrediting the mortals, intimidating them, and moving on.<br /> #5 Allies [everything] 5 should do the trick. Alternatively, choose a curse, any relevant social curse. You won't have to use it for long.<br /> <br /> That said, a social Mage should expect to hit a lot of Wisdom Breaking Points.<br /> <br /> Vampires<br /> #1 Dominate 1, Majesty 2, Obfuscate 1, Protean 3, Celerity 1, Nightmare 1, Nughmare 2, Nightmare 3 all potentially solve this problem.<br /> #2 Blood Bonds and/or Majesty are built for this. Nightmare 3 can do it. Auspex can assist with mundane social rolls. Vampires are made for this.<br /> #3 Dominate 1 or 3, Majesty 2, Nightmare 3 and a Blood Bond can solve this problem. Be careful with Blood Bonds! It could backfire and make him obsessed.<br /> #4 Dominate 1 can rewrite their short term memories. Majesty 2 or Nightmare 3 can feed them a story, make them seem insane, or otherwise help discredit them. Relevant allies can help.<br /> #5 Need relevant allies. Dominate 3, Majesty 2+, Nightmare 3, and Blood Bonds can turn their social structures against them. Auspex will know all the weak points even at 1, though 2 will help exploit them. Animalism gets a special mention because there are few business an intense roach infestation won't shut down.<br /> <br /> Note that Auspex is a powerful support tool for social and would aid any of the above, especially supplementing the mortal strategies. An Auspex social character needs to be a good social character, whole Majesty / Dominate can buy up Allies instead of fast talk and sympathetic (I would still get Sympathetic).<br /> <br /> -----<br /> <br /> So what if a Vampire is applying social power to a Mage? Direct supernatural influence will ping on Mage Sight, but they won't be able to trace the magic back to the Vampire easily. The Vampire wants to work as far away and indirectly as possible. Majesty user's and Nightmare user's will screw themselves. Dominate (thoroughly erase memories), Obfuscate, Auspex, and Animalism is the way to go.<br /> <br /> That said, if the scenario is a Mage being tee' d off at a Vampire socially, they can just drop the hammer and there isn't much that the Vampire can do to stop it, especially if the Mage doesn't care about Wisdom loss. Vampires with Cruac 1 can always find out who is messing with them. Auspex 2 or 3 *might* point the Vampire in the right direction.<br /> <br /> Both work on offense. Mages have better defense in the form of Mage Sight and Shielding Spells. Really, it comes down to which one targeted the other first. Even then, if the other found out i would be a bitter fight until one died or there was nothing left.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1157,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","user":"SoulGambit","date":". 09-06-2017, 11:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-06T13:23:17-07:00","id":1138090,"title":"","content":"So! Let's do Combat, because that is everyone's favorite theory field.<br /> <br /> Generally speaking, combat vampires will have Protean 3 (+Swarm Form), Obfuscate 3, Celerity 3, or Celerity 1 + Resilience/Vigor 2<br /> <br /> Mages will come from one of three schools of thought.<br /> A) Combat Magic. This character will probably get Shadow Name 3 + Themed Cabal and/or some combat spells as Rotes.<br /> B) All the Buffs.<br /> C) Who cares about Paradox?<br /> <br /> Going BP 2 / Gnosis 2 is almost definately the best investment for a character, but I will be ignoring that. I am also going to ignore Professional Training 5 for Rote combat dice, but not Destiny as it is a Mage Specific benefit. I will also ignore minions like ghouls and ghosts and spirits, as that is a different catagory.<br /> <br /> Mage' s tools in a white room<br /> - Exceptional Luck can be used Reflexively to either curse an opponent (if you can get above their Withstand) or, more usefully, bless yourself with Steadfast and +1 (or more) Potency so your spells automatically work.<br /> - Direct Damage is dealing Bashing and, more importantly, inflicting tilts. You need it to be a Rote to be effective at Arcana 3. That will let you Instant Cast, Perception Range, and inflict a Tilt without risking Paradox. You deal 3B base and can probably take -4 for another +2B, or with Steadfast -8 for +4B. Willpower will allow for another +1B or +2B. That will stun everyone who doesn't have Resilience.<br /> - Forces can deal Agg with a lighter, probably 3-5 agg (an Inferno will deal too much collateral in most instances) per turn.<br /> - Forces 3 during a thunderstorm can deal straight 10B.<br /> - Space 3, Matter 2/3 can permanently trap someone. The only real counterplay is Protean 1 or Vigor 2 for matter and... There simply isn't a counter for Space. Time 3 can completely disable someone by turning them into an infant. Mental Domination and Sleep of the Just work at Mind 2 and 3, respectively.<br /> <br /> If a Mage uses Yantras, a Vampire can probably justify using a Celerity Interrupt. What this means is that some starting Mages can win some of the time if they get off their spells without Yantras (Exceptional Luck rote is neigh essential) or against Vampires without Celerity even if they do. If a Vampire has any Anti-Magic merits and/or has Giant Size things get trickier.<br /> <br /> A buffmage is going to be a lot trickier to analyze since there are multiple moving parts. First, a Mage can *not* walk around with obvious magic like attributes above 5 or constant acceleration, and in combat a buff you put up means you didn't spend that action disabling all of your opponents. I'll ruminate on what combination (s) of buffs are available at creation.<br /> <br /> EDIT:<br /> <br /> Having thought about it, in a white room two characters see each other type scenario, the Vampire with Celerity wins against lower level Mages most if not all the time.<br /> <br /> Let's say the Mage goes first. Either they are using Yantras, on which case the Vampire can Celerity Interrupt to dodge out of the way / be invisible for the spell, or they don't. A Mage going for a one hit kill will probably Steadfast themselves and not use a Yantra, but it doesn't matter. The Vampire interrupts their turn no matter what they are doing to initiate a grapple. Once in a grapple, the Mage can not effectively use Yantras or cast without them. If the Grapple fails, then the Mage probably wins. Now a counterplay here for the Mage is to use Exceptional Luck to reflexively debuff the Vampire, inflicting Leg Wrack x2. The issue is, the Mage will probably only have Fate 2 and if they use any form of Yantra the Vampire can interrupt *that* instead of the other one.<br /> <br /> If the Vampire wins, they use Celerity to launch a surprise attack, during which they can not be seen and thus can not be targeted by perception spells.<br /> <br /> The question becomes, can the Mage just brute force the Grapple directly? With the Mage having Destiny? It's very possible they could just overpower the Vampire, break free, then cast their combat ending spell. If they won initiative, that would be it. If they didn't, then they probably need to do it twice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1157,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","user":"SoulGambit","date":". 09-07-2017, 10:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-06T13:30:09-07:00","id":1138096,"title":"","content":"Double post boo","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1157,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","user":"SoulGambit","date":". 09-06-2017, 04:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-07T08:50:14-07:00","id":1138331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1136212-vampire-vs-mages?p=1138090#post1138090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So! Let's do Combat, because that is everyone's favorite theory field.<br /> <br /> Generally speaking, combat vampires will have Protean 3 (+Swarm Form), Obfuscate 3, Celerity 3, or Celerity 1 + Resilience/Vigor 2<br /> <br /> Mages will come from one of three schools of thought.<br /> A) Combat Magic. This character will probably get Shadow Name 3 + Themed Cabal and/or some combat spells as Rotes.<br /> B) All the Buffs.<br /> C) Who cares about Paradox?<br /> <br /> Going BP 2 / Gnosis 2 is almost def